@startuml sequence_diagram_list
autonumber
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
title Sequence Diagram - BCK10 List Predefined Pizzas for Management

actor Manager
participant Routes as "PredefinedPizzaRoutes / Express"
participant Auth as "AuthMiddleware (BCK01)"
participant Roles as "RoleMiddleware (BCK01)"
participant Controller as "PredefinedPizzaController"
participant Service as "PredefinedPizzaManagementService"
participant ProductRepository as "ProductRepository (BCK05)"
participant Mapper as "PredefinedPizzaResponseMapper"
database DB as "PostgreSQL"

Manager -> Routes : GET /api/v1/predefined-pizzas
Routes -> Auth : verifyToken(req)
Auth --> Routes : next() with authenticated req.user
Routes -> Roles : requireRole(MANAGER)
Roles --> Routes : next() when authorized
Routes -> Controller : list(req, res)
Controller -> Service : list()
Service -> ProductRepository : listPredefinedPizzas()
ProductRepository -> DB : SELECT component-based Sellable Products with composition
DB --> ProductRepository : Product rows and composition items
ProductRepository --> Service : configured PredefinedPizza Products
loop each configured Product
  Service -> Mapper : toDTO(Product)
  Mapper --> Service : { id, componentIds }
end
Service --> Controller : response DTO list
Controller --> Manager : 200 OK + array (empty if none are configured)

note over Manager,DB
  The list contains configured component-based Sellable Products only.
  It returns the shared Product ID and default composition. BCK11 owns
  customer-facing prices and current size availability. Authentication,
  authorization or repository errors are forwarded through Express to the
  global handler and mapped to the shared JSON error response.
end note
@enduml
